## Structure (modular monolith)

```
src/
├── modules/<module>/            ← each module is a full vertical slice
│   ├── <module>.module.ts       ← NestJS module (exports public API)
│   ├── <module>.controller.ts   ← HTTP layer
│   ├── <module>.service.ts      ← business logic
│   ├── <module>.repository.ts   ← data access (branched by ORM)
│   ├── entities/<module>.entity.ts
│   ├── dto/create-<module>.dto.ts
│   └── <module>.controller.spec.ts
└── shared/                      ← shared kernel (cross-cutting)
    ├── database/                ← ORM clients
    ├── cache/                   ← Redis
    ├── auth/                    ← guards, interceptors
    └── health/                  ← health check
```

**Module boundaries:** each module exposes a public API through its
`*.module.ts` `exports` array. Other modules import only that public
surface — never reach into another module's internal files directly.

**Shared kernel:** `src/shared/` contains infrastructure code that every
module can depend on. It must never depend on a feature module.

